    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūmesco</span></b>  (less correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hū-</span></b> ), no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i> nor <i>sup.</i>, ĕre, 3, <i>v.
				inch. n.</i> [umeo], <i>to grow moist</i> or <i>wet</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(equi) umescunt spumis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 111</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cortex non umescit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 14, 24, § 107</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra umescens rore occulto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					18, 34, 77, § 339</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Sept. 10, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vidimus umescentes oculos tuos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Pan. 73, 4</span></i>
			. </div>
